# A17 item 1 (R38 N2) — the auction-create negative leg, NOT PROVEN (infra-limited; recorded honestly). The mechanism: the pinned wallet derives its next address at a clock-based index (now + 2817325936, skipping indices it exposed itself — zcash_client_sqlite get_next_available_address), so a burst of generations pins the next generated index deterministically and a real dust note there must make 'benzo auction create' refuse it.
# Five attempts (600 / 2400 / 2400 / 4800 / 9000 generations), each run with: node tmp/r38-n2.mjs (tools/repro/r38-n2.ts). Outside causes only: today's testnet mined each dust 20-90 minutes after broadcast (attempt logs tmp/r38-n2-run.log, overwritten per attempt) and the burst itself degrades superlinearly as the wallet's exposed-address table grows (4.1 -> 1.7 generations/s), so the determinism window closes before the dust is visible. The last attempt's own output is below.
